{"type":"text","timestamp":1780750093056,"sessionID":"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo","part":{"id":"prt_e9cf9f737001NYUU7pp6aTFFO0","messageID":"msg_e9cf9dfd0001bvRJfAX4pcjTGk","sessionID":"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo","type":"text","text":"The Phase 6 contract is readable and declares the component role union `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`; I’m checking the Phase 6 workflow rules and the current touched source files against that set before writing the report.","time":{"start":1780750087991,"end":1780750093051},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0e2676025ddb8b78016a241707f2248190811c712acb1b645d","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780750093167,"sessionID":"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_RvNudXlmQkQT7X5h6x5TWhTA","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md","offset":520,"limit":2200},"output":"<path>/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n520: - Loop primitive: `~/ai/tools/coderabbit_review_driver.py review-loop ${repo} ${pr_num} --worktree-path ${worktree_path} --mode ${coderabbit_trigger_mode}`.\n521: - The driver owns the full loop: trigger or auto-skip an already-pending trigger, wait for ack, enforce the 300-second minimum cadence between loop-owned polls, dispatch one fixer invocation per actionable in-diff comment, preserve each structured outcome, push fixed commits, post reply files, trigger incremental follow-up reviews, and continue until terminal.\n522: - `terminal_reason=approved` is CodeRabbit success.\n523: - `terminal_reason=no_value_provided` is accepted convergence when every actionable in-diff comment in the latest iteration was assessed `review_provided_value: false`.\n524: - `needs_caller_decision=true` surfaces valuable `rejected` or `deferred` per-comment outcomes to the root caller without re-triggering.\n525: - The orchestrator must not compose its own trigger/poll/dispatch/retrigger loop, must not use inline `gh pr view ... statusCheckRollup` polling, must not inline CodeRabbit comment bodies, and must not synthesize an empty review pass.\n526: - If the pipeline creates or reuses a PR, it writes `${scratch_dir}/pr-url.txt`; Phase 9 reuses that URL instead of creating a duplicate PR.\n527: \n528: ## Phase 8 - Post-Review Gates\n529: \n530: - These are the PR-opening gates on the actual diff.\n531: - Policy: dispatch `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` after Phase 7 readiness and optional review delegation, before draft PR movement.\n532: - The Phase 8 gate-set inventory is test-audit review, multi-concern PR review, justification PR review, commit hygiene, Phase 8 actual-diff code-quality, proof-risk and validation-integrity runtime-claim transport where applicable, supported-surface inventory-resolution while ACR-286 remains open, currentness rechecks against prior joins, `${planning_dir}/risk/phase-8-join-manifest.json`, and process-tree audit #3.\n533: - Rule: the actual PR diff is the review target. Proposal-shaped evidence cannot satisfy actual-diff rows.\n534: - Rule: `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` writes or verifies the Phase 8 join manifest at `${planning_dir}/risk/phase-8-join-manifest.json`, projects expected-process evidence, and requires process-tree audit #3 evidence. Rows carry at least `canonical_output_path`, `size`, `mtime`, `sha256`, `verdict_line`, and `verified_at`, plus the operator schema's caller mode, raw/normalized verdict, applicability, currentness, inventory-resolution, and blocking-status fields. Currentness rechecks against prior joins follow `~/ai/conventions/apply-gate-set-currentness.md` § `Currentness key schema`, § `Row-level re-verification`, and § `Full re-dispatch`.\n535: - Rule: the Phase 8 code-quality rows must carry actual-diff runtime-claim context under the Phase 3 `## Proof plan` rule. Validation-integrity and proof-risk remain required where that context makes them applicable.\n536: - Rule: if the multi-concern row says the diff should be split, split it before opening PRs.\n537: - Rule: preserve ACR-280 Phase 8 code-quality strategy selection. For current semantic Phase 8 code-quality `MEDIUM` or `HIGH`, choose MOVE-and-import and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_MOVE_AND_IMPORT`, in-place file-decomposition and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_FILE_DECOMPOSITION`, in-WU remediation/helper extraction and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_INWU`, or follow-up-ticket decomposition and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_FOLLOWUP`. Follow-up tickets require current-WU narrowing and rerun or explicit `DECOMPOSED`; they never allow advance by themselves.\n538: - Rule: only a returned `PASS` from `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` permits closure judge dispatch, draft PR creation, ticket comment work, or PR movement. `BLOCKED`, `NEEDS_INPUT`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `STALE_REFUSAL`, stale rows, missing output paths, malformed manifests, or process-tree blocking findings prevent draft PR creation until the affected subtree is rerun or repaired.\n539: - Rule: if a delegated agent returns `NEEDS_INPUT:<question_artifact>`, the root handles it through `~/ai/conventions/agent-questions-and-session-graph.md`. Do not advance this phase, write code, post review output, or open a PR from work that depends on the unanswered question.\n540: - Phase 8 is the review and capture layer that precedes draft PR creation; it is not followed by a human branch-local review fallback before Phase 9.\n541: - Phase 8 capture documentation: after `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` returns `PASS` with process-tree audit #3 evidence cleared, the orchestrator dispatches the `gpt-xhigh` closure judge and records `actual_story_points` and `actual_capture_method` as an orchestrator-owned closure artifact before Phase 9. The enum is `closer-best-effort | wall-time-derived | unmeasured`, the point set is `1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 40, 100`, and wall-time-derived is reserved as enum-only with no requirements for timers, durations, start/stop timestamps, or trace-derived time calculations.\n542: - Rule: ACR-125 capture must not dispatch `task=update-estimate` for actuals, must not write actuals to Linear `estimate`, and must not write actuals to Jira `customfield_10016`; live ticket estimate fields continue to hold the refined estimate.\n543: - Final verification-only behavior: Final does not recalculate the actual; it verifies the audit-history calibration block and `estimate_comparison_comment_ref`, then references the comparison in the close-comment.\n544: - Final halt-on-missing: on a missing/invalid/inconsistent calibration block or invalid `estimate_comparison_comment_ref`, Final halts and must not post the close-comment. Final verification accepts `<id | url | none>`, rejects `path`, and treats none valid only when `ticket_system: jira`. On success, Final close-comment includes inherited/refined/actual values inline on both backends.\n545: \n546: ```worked example\n547: Phase 8 worked example\n548: \n549: inherited_story_point_estimate: 3\n550: refined_story_point_estimate: 5\n551: actual_story_points: 8\n552: actual_capture_method: closer-best-effort\n553: estimate_delta_narrative: inherited=3; refined=5; actual=8; delta_refined_to_actual=3; over_2x_inherited=true\n554: \n555: sample comment body\n556: \n557: Estimate calibration\n558: \n559: - inherited_story_point_estimate: 3\n560: - refined_story_point_estimate: 5\n561: - actual_story_points: 8\n562: - actual_capture_method: closer-best-effort\n563: - actual_estimate_rationale: closer-best-effort: closure scope landed broader than the refined estimate assumed.\n564: - estimate_delta_narrative: inherited=3; refined=5; actual=8; delta_refined_to_actual=3; over_2x_inherited=true\n565: - audit_history: ${planning_dir}/audit-history.md\n566: ```\n567: \n568: ## Phase 9 - Draft PR\n569: \n570: - Routine automation step after all prior gates pass.\n571: - Rule: if Phase 7 wrote `${scratch_dir}/pr-url.txt`, Phase 9 verifies and reuses that PR instead of running `gh pr create` again.\n572: - Rule: open one draft PR per concern identified by multi-concern review.\n573: - Rule: respect dependency order for stacked work.\n574: - Rule: follow `~/ai/conventions/git.md`.\n575: - Rule: opening a **draft** PR is not Tier-3 by default.\n576: - Rule: **the title and body MUST be authored by `~/ai/agents/pr-writer.md`** — never hand-written by the orchestrator and never inlined into the `gh pr create` invocation. The writer enforces audience-and-content rules (no internal jargon, no commit-history sections, no closed-PR or local-planning-artifact references) that hand-written or templated bodies routinely violate. Pass the relevant phase artifacts (`problem-map.md`, `proposal.md`, `contract.md`, RCA evidence) as `context_files` so the writer has intent grounding without citing them in the body. For stacked PRs, supply `stack_parent_pr=<num>`; for any reference to merged work, supply `merged_refs=<list>`; when the selected ticket backend is Linear and the Linear key is known, supply `linear_issue_keys=<KEY>` so `pr-writer` emits the close-keyword footer itself.\n577: - Rule: RCA-track. The draft PR description includes before/after evidence for every Phase 0 red signal, whether a newly authored reproduction test or an existing failing test accepted as the reproduction signal: the red-run command and output or accepted failure evidence, paired with the matching post-fix green-run command and output recorded in Step 6c. Pass the evidence path(s) to `pr-writer` via `context_files` so they're folded into the body in audience-safe form.\n578: \n579: ## Phase 10 - Promote To Ready-For-Review\n580: \n581: - Automated by the orchestrator once Phase 9 succeeds and the Phase 8 process-tree audit has cleared.\n582: - Rule: the orchestrator runs `gh pr ready <pr_number>` and records the promotion in `${scratch_dir}/pr-promoted.txt`. No human gate.\n583: \n584: ## Gate Ownership\n585: \n586: See `~/ai/conventions/gate-ownership.md` for the phase-by-phase table.\n587: \n588: Rule of thumb:\n589: - the implementation-pipeline human gates are (1) the Phase 2.5 problem-map review and (2) legitimate NEEDS_INPUT new-value-question surfacing per `~/ai/agents/implementation-pipeline-orchestrator.md`\n590: - every other phase belongs to a model gate or to automation\n591: - the proposal is reviewed by the risk gate, not by an extra human approval pass\n592: - Phase 9 (draft PR) and Phase 10 (promotion) are both automated by the orchestrator\n593: \n594: ## Tiered Approval\n595: \n596: Anything with user-visible side effects follows `~/ai/workflows/tiered-approval.md`.\n597: \n598: Practical default:\n599: - drafting code is not Tier-3\n600: - editing files is not Tier-3\n601: - running tests is not Tier-3\n602: - opening **draft** PRs is not Tier-3\n603: - public promotion and other outward-facing actions follow the tiered-approval workflow\n604: \n605: ## Pause For Refactor\n606: \n607: This section owns the pause state model for existing-code refactor work discovered during an implementation WU. For the strategy boundary, cite `conventions/feature-development-workflow.md` `## Refactoring out of scope`; do not restate that rule elsewhere in this workflow.\n608: \n609: - trigger: an auditor, reviewer, or implementation step identifies existing-code structural refactor work that is outside touched-file/component ownership, or inside touched ownership but too large for the current WU, and material to continuing safely.\n610: - pause evidence: record the current ticket id, branch, head SHA, worktree path, dirty status, failing or residual report paths, and the reason the refactor is outside touched ownership or requires decomposition.\n611: - ticket/backend action: use the selected ticket backend to comment the pause evidence on the current ticket and apply the available pause/blocking status or label; if no status exists, use a clear blocking comment plus link relation.\n612: - refactor-ticket filing: file a linked refactor-ticket with the bounded structural target, preserved-behavior requirement, evidence paths, and relationship to the paused WU.\n613: - ACR-179 routing: run the refactor-ticket through the ACR-179 refactoring route, using `workflows/refactoring.md` and `agents/refactoring-orchestrator.md`.\n614: - resume: resume the paused WU only after the refactor-ticket is closed, superseded, or explicitly dispositioned by the active manager flavor with recorded evidence.\n615: - touched-file/component gate failures: this pause path does not alter touched-file/component ownership; current-WU `MEDIUM` or `HIGH` code-quality findings still revise, remediate, or decompose under the existing LOW-only rules.\n616: \n617: ## Decision Recording\n618: \n619: <!-- INTENTIONAL: \"deferred\" here is a decision-recording state category, not an unwired workflow stub. -->\n620: If a phase is skipped, narrowed, deferred, terminated for non-positive value, sent back to research on invalidated assumptions, or accepted with a named unverifiable residual risk that does not collapse the approved net-value case under the supported-surface termination rule:\n621: - record it in `${worktree_path}/DECISIONS.md` or an explicitly supplied project equivalent\n622: - record who made the decision\n623: - record why the change was accepted\n624: - record what risk is being accepted\n625: - record what evidence caused the termination or research re-entry\n626: \n627: For Phase 6 firstness, do not create a new residual class. If a named test-verification risk remains unverified, record it in `risk/NN-test-residuals.md`. If only historical or process-provenance evidence is unverifiable and the approved net-value case still holds, record the decision only as `accepted with a named unverifiable residual risk` in `${worktree_path}/DECISIONS.md` or an explicitly supplied project equivalent.\n628: \n629: Accepted halt residuals and accepted `auditor_verdict_conflict_residual` entries follow this same Decision Recording rule when they do not collapse the approved net-value case.\n630: \n631: Decision Recording, generic residual recording, and Phase 7 / Phase 8 residual / value-zero review language do NOT authorize residual acceptance of Phase 4 code-quality, Phase 6 prototype-risk, or per-component code-quality `MEDIUM` or `HIGH` verdicts. Those gate verdicts revise, remediate, or decompose per `~/ai/conventions/code-quality.md` § `Disposition policy` and § `Oscillation signals WU-too-large`; they are never recorded as residuals. Generic residual recording remains valid for non-gate residual classes only (bounded test-verification residuals in `risk/NN-test-residuals.md`, process-provenance uncertainty per the Phase 6 firstness paragraph above, accepted halt residuals, accepted `auditor_verdict_conflict_residual` entries, and Phase 8 value-zero termination evidence).\n632: \n633: Without that record, the phase was not skipped correctly.\n634: \n635: ## Orchestrator\n636: \n637: This pipeline is dispatched by the `implementation-pipeline-orchestrator` (`gpt-xhigh`) operator at `~/ai/agents/implementation-pipeline-orchestrator.md`. The orchestrator is the only delegated actor that walks a Work Unit through every phase, dispatches each leaf operator via the `agents` CLI, runs the three required process-tree audits, and enforces the violation-escalation policy autonomously (including Tier-1 main-branch rewinds when a violation is detected). Inlining the orchestrator role into the root conversation is itself a workflow violation because it removes the orchestration decisions from `agents trace --json` and prevents process-tree-auditor from auditing the workflow as a whole.\n638: \n639: ## Adjacent References\n640: \n641: - `~/ai/agents/implementation-pipeline-orchestrator.md`\n642: - `~/ai/models/roles.md`\n643: - `~/ai/workflows/agents-cli.md`\n644: - `~/ai/conventions/worktree-isolation.md`\n645: - `~/ai/conventions/git.md`\n646: - `~/ai/agents/coderabbit-operator.md`\n647: - `~/ai/workflows/pr-review.md`\n648: - `~/ai/workflows/tiered-approval.md`\n649: - `~/ai/conventions/no-backwards-compatibility.md`\n650: - `~/ai/conventions/no-deferred-stubs.md`\n651: - `~/ai/conventions/gate-ownership.md`\n652: - `~/ai/conventions/audit-history.md`\n\n(End of file - total 652 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"- Loop primitive: `~/ai/tools/coderabbit_review_driver.py review-loop ${repo} ${pr_num} --worktree-path ${worktree_path} --mode ${coderabbit_trigger_mode}`.\n- The driver owns the full loop: trigger or auto-skip an already-pending trigger, wait for ack, enforce the 300-second minimum cadence between loop-owned polls, dispatch one fixer invocation per actionable in-diff comment, preserve each structured outcome, push fixed commits, post reply files, trigger incremental follow-up reviews, and continue until terminal.\n- `terminal_reason=approved` is CodeRabbit success.\n- `terminal_reason=no_value_provided` is accepted convergence when every actionable in-diff comment in the latest iteration was assessed `review_provided_value: false`.\n- `needs_caller_decision=true` surfaces valuable `rejected` or `deferred` per-comment outcomes to the root caller without re-triggering.\n- The orchestrator must not compose its own trigger/poll/dispatch/retrigger loop, must not use inline `gh pr view ... statusCheckRollup` polling, must not inline CodeRabbit comment bodies, and must not synthesize an empty review pass.\n- If the pipeline creates or reuses a PR, it writes `${scratch_dir}/pr-url.txt`; Phase 9 reuses that URL instead of creating a duplicate PR.\n\n## Phase 8 - Post-Review Gates\n\n- These are the PR-opening gates on the actual diff.\n- Policy: dispatch `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` after Phase 7 readiness and optional review delegation, before draft PR movement.\n- The Phase 8 gate-set inventory is test-audit review, multi-concern PR review, justification PR review, commit hygiene, Phase 8 actual-diff code-quality, proof-risk and validation-integrity runtime-claim transport where applicable, supported-surface inventory-resolution while ACR-286 remains open, currentness rechecks against prior joins, `${planning_dir}/risk/phase-8-join-manifest.json`, and process-tree audit #3.\n- Rule: the actual PR diff is the review target. Proposal-shaped evidence cannot satisfy actual-diff rows.\n- Rule: `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` writes or verifies the Phase 8 join manifest at `${planning_dir}/risk/phase-8-join-manifest.json`, projects expected-process evidence, and requires process-tree audit #3 evidence. Rows carry at least `canonical_output_path`, `size`, `mtime`, `sha256`, `verdict_line`, and `verified_at`, plus the operator schema's caller mode, raw/normalized verdict, applicability, currentness, inventory-resolution, and blocking-status fields. Currentness rechecks against prior joins follow `~/ai/conventions/apply-gate-set-currentness.md` § `Currentness key schema`, § `Row-level re-verification`, and § `Full re-dispatch`.\n- Rule: the Phase 8 code-quality rows must carry actual-diff runtime-claim context under the Phase 3 `## Proof plan` rule. Validation-integrity and proof-risk remain required where that context makes them applicable.\n- Rule: if the multi-concern row says the diff should be split, split it before opening PRs.\n- Rule: preserve ACR-280 Phase 8 code-quality strategy selection. For current semantic Phase 8 code-quality `MEDIUM` or `HIGH`, choose MOVE-and-import and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_MOVE_AND_IMPORT`, in-place file-decomposition and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_FILE_DECOMPOSITION`, in-WU remediation/helper extraction and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_INWU`, or follow-up-ticket decomposition and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_FOLLOWUP`. Follow-up tickets require current-WU narrowing and rerun or explicit `DECOMPOSED`; they never allow advance by themselves.\n- Rule: only a returned `PASS` from `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` permits closure judge dispatch, draft PR creation, ticket comment work, or PR movement. `BLOCKED`, `NEEDS_INPUT`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `STALE_REFUSAL`, stale rows, missing output paths, malformed manifests, or process-tree blocking findings prevent draft PR creation until the affected subtree is rerun or repaired.\n- Rule: if a delegated agent returns `NEEDS_INPUT:<question_artifact>`, the root handles it through `~/ai/conventions/agent-questions-and-session-graph.md`. Do not advance this phase, write code, post review output, or open a PR from work that depends on the unanswered question.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md","text":"- Loop primitive: `~/ai/tools/coderabbit_review_driver.py review-loop ${repo} ${pr_num} --worktree-path ${worktree_path} --mode ${coderabbit_trigger_mode}`.\n- The driver owns the full loop: trigger or auto-skip an already-pending trigger, wait for ack, enforce the 300-second minimum cadence between loop-owned polls, dispatch one fixer invocation per actionable in-diff comment, preserve each structured outcome, push fixed commits, post reply files, trigger incremental follow-up reviews, and continue until terminal.\n- `terminal_reason=approved` is CodeRabbit success.\n- `terminal_reason=no_value_provided` is accepted convergence when every actionable in-diff comment in the latest iteration was assessed `review_provided_value: false`.\n- `needs_caller_decision=true` surfaces valuable `rejected` or `deferred` per-comment outcomes to the root caller without re-triggering.\n- The orchestrator must not compose its own trigger/poll/dispatch/retrigger loop, must not use inline `gh pr view ... statusCheckRollup` polling, must not inline CodeRabbit comment bodies, and must not synthesize an empty review pass.\n- If the pipeline creates or reuses a PR, it writes `${scratch_dir}/pr-url.txt`; Phase 9 reuses that URL instead of creating a duplicate PR.\n\n## Phase 8 - Post-Review Gates\n\n- These are the PR-opening gates on the actual diff.\n- Policy: dispatch `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` after Phase 7 readiness and optional review delegation, before draft PR movement.\n- The Phase 8 gate-set inventory is test-audit review, multi-concern PR review, justification PR review, commit hygiene, Phase 8 actual-diff code-quality, proof-risk and validation-integrity runtime-claim transport where applicable, supported-surface inventory-resolution while ACR-286 remains open, currentness rechecks against prior joins, `${planning_dir}/risk/phase-8-join-manifest.json`, and process-tree audit #3.\n- Rule: the actual PR diff is the review target. Proposal-shaped evidence cannot satisfy actual-diff rows.\n- Rule: `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` writes or verifies the Phase 8 join manifest at `${planning_dir}/risk/phase-8-join-manifest.json`, projects expected-process evidence, and requires process-tree audit #3 evidence. Rows carry at least `canonical_output_path`, `size`, `mtime`, `sha256`, `verdict_line`, and `verified_at`, plus the operator schema's caller mode, raw/normalized verdict, applicability, currentness, inventory-resolution, and blocking-status fields. Currentness rechecks against prior joins follow `~/ai/conventions/apply-gate-set-currentness.md` § `Currentness key schema`, § `Row-level re-verification`, and § `Full re-dispatch`.\n- Rule: the Phase 8 code-quality rows must carry actual-diff runtime-claim context under the Phase 3 `## Proof plan` rule. Validation-integrity and proof-risk remain required where that context makes them applicable.\n- Rule: if the multi-concern row says the diff should be split, split it before opening PRs.\n- Rule: preserve ACR-280 Phase 8 code-quality strategy selection. For current semantic Phase 8 code-quality `MEDIUM` or `HIGH`, choose MOVE-and-import and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_MOVE_AND_IMPORT`, in-place file-decomposition and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_FILE_DECOMPOSITION`, in-WU remediation/helper extraction and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_INWU`, or follow-up-ticket decomposition and record `STRATEGY_PHASE8_CODE_QUALITY_FOLLOWUP`. Follow-up tickets require current-WU narrowing and rerun or explicit `DECOMPOSED`; they never allow advance by themselves.\n- Rule: only a returned `PASS` from `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` permits closure judge dispatch, draft PR creation, ticket comment work, or PR movement. `BLOCKED`, `NEEDS_INPUT`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `STALE_REFUSAL`, stale rows, missing output paths, malformed manifests, or process-tree blocking findings prevent draft PR creation until the affected subtree is rerun or repaired.\n- Rule: if a delegated agent returns `NEEDS_INPUT:<question_artifact>`, the root handles it through `~/ai/conventions/agent-questions-and-session-graph.md`. Do not advance this phase, write code, post review output, or open a PR from work that depends on the unanswered question.\n- Phase 8 is the review and capture layer that precedes draft PR creation; it is not followed by a human branch-local review fallback before Phase 9.\n- Phase 8 capture documentation: after `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` returns `PASS` with process-tree audit #3 evidence cleared, the orchestrator dispatches the `gpt-xhigh` closure judge and records `actual_story_points` and `actual_capture_method` as an orchestrator-owned closure artifact before Phase 9. The enum is `closer-best-effort | wall-time-derived | unmeasured`, the point set is `1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, 21, 40, 100`, and wall-time-derived is reserved as enum-only with no requirements for timers, durations, start/stop timestamps, or trace-derived time calculations.\n- Rule: ACR-125 capture must not dispatch `task=update-estimate` for actuals, must not write actuals to Linear `estimate`, and must not write actuals to Jira `customfield_10016`; live ticket estimate fields continue to hold the refined estimate.\n- Final verification-only behavior: Final does not recalculate the actual; it verifies the audit-history calibration block and `estimate_comparison_comment_ref`, then references the comparison in the close-comment.\n- Final halt-on-missing: on a missing/invalid/inconsistent calibration block or invalid `estimate_comparison_comment_ref`, Final halts and must not post the close-comment. Final verification accepts `<id | url | none>`, rejects `path`, and treats none valid only when `ticket_system: jira`. On success, Final close-comment includes inherited/refined/actual values inline on both backends.\n\n```worked example\nPhase 8 worked example\n\ninherited_story_point_estimate: 3\nrefined_story_point_estimate: 5\nactual_story_points: 8\nactual_capture_method: closer-best-effort\nestimate_delta_narrative: inherited=3; refined=5; actual=8; delta_refined_to_actual=3; over_2x_inherited=true\n\nsample comment body\n\nEstimate calibration\n\n- inherited_story_point_estimate: 3\n- refined_story_point_estimate: 5\n- actual_story_points: 8\n- actual_capture_method: closer-best-effort\n- actual_estimate_rationale: closer-best-effort: closure scope landed broader than the refined estimate assumed.\n- estimate_delta_narrative: inherited=3; refined=5; actual=8; delta_refined_to_actual=3; over_2x_inherited=true\n- audit_history: ${planning_dir}/audit-history.md\n```\n\n## Phase 9 - Draft PR\n\n- Routine automation step after all prior gates pass.\n- Rule: if Phase 7 wrote `${scratch_dir}/pr-url.txt`, Phase 9 verifies and reuses that PR instead of running `gh pr create` again.\n- Rule: open one draft PR per concern identified by multi-concern review.\n- Rule: respect dependency order for stacked work.\n- Rule: follow `~/ai/conventions/git.md`.\n- Rule: opening a **draft** PR is not Tier-3 by default.\n- Rule: **the title and body MUST be authored by `~/ai/agents/pr-writer.md`** — never hand-written by the orchestrator and never inlined into the `gh pr create` invocation. The writer enforces audience-and-content rules (no internal jargon, no commit-history sections, no closed-PR or local-planning-artifact references) that hand-written or templated bodies routinely violate. Pass the relevant phase artifacts (`problem-map.md`, `proposal.md`, `contract.md`, RCA evidence) as `context_files` so the writer has intent grounding without citing them in the body. For stacked PRs, supply `stack_parent_pr=<num>`; for any reference to merged work, supply `merged_refs=<list>`; when the selected ticket backend is Linear and the Linear key is known, supply `linear_issue_keys=<KEY>` so `pr-writer` emits the close-keyword footer itself.\n- Rule: RCA-track. The draft PR description includes before/after evidence for every Phase 0 red signal, whether a newly authored reproduction test or an existing failing test accepted as the reproduction signal: the red-run command and output or accepted failure evidence, paired with the matching post-fix green-run command and output recorded in Step 6c. Pass the evidence path(s) to `pr-writer` via `context_files` so they're folded into the body in audience-safe form.\n\n## Phase 10 - Promote To Ready-For-Review\n\n- Automated by the orchestrator once Phase 9 succeeds and the Phase 8 process-tree audit has cleared.\n- Rule: the orchestrator runs `gh pr ready <pr_number>` and records the promotion in `${scratch_dir}/pr-promoted.txt`. No human gate.\n\n## Gate Ownership\n\nSee `~/ai/conventions/gate-ownership.md` for the phase-by-phase table.\n\nRule of thumb:\n- the implementation-pipeline human gates are (1) the Phase 2.5 problem-map review and (2) legitimate NEEDS_INPUT new-value-question surfacing per `~/ai/agents/implementation-pipeline-orchestrator.md`\n- every other phase belongs to a model gate or to automation\n- the proposal is reviewed by the risk gate, not by an extra human approval pass\n- Phase 9 (draft PR) and Phase 10 (promotion) are both automated by the orchestrator\n\n## Tiered Approval\n\nAnything with user-visible side effects follows `~/ai/workflows/tiered-approval.md`.\n\nPractical default:\n- drafting code is not Tier-3\n- editing files is not Tier-3\n- running tests is not Tier-3\n- opening **draft** PRs is not Tier-3\n- public promotion and other outward-facing actions follow the tiered-approval workflow\n\n## Pause For Refactor\n\nThis section owns the pause state model for existing-code refactor work discovered during an implementation WU. For the strategy boundary, cite `conventions/feature-development-workflow.md` `## Refactoring out of scope`; do not restate that rule elsewhere in this workflow.\n\n- trigger: an auditor, reviewer, or implementation step identifies existing-code structural refactor work that is outside touched-file/component ownership, or inside touched ownership but too large for the current WU, and material to continuing safely.\n- pause evidence: record the current ticket id, branch, head SHA, worktree path, dirty status, failing or residual report paths, and the reason the refactor is outside touched ownership or requires decomposition.\n- ticket/backend action: use the selected ticket backend to comment the pause evidence on the current ticket and apply the available pause/blocking status or label; if no status exists, use a clear blocking comment plus link relation.\n- refactor-ticket filing: file a linked refactor-ticket with the bounded structural target, preserved-behavior requirement, evidence paths, and relationship to the paused WU.\n- ACR-179 routing: run the refactor-ticket through the ACR-179 refactoring route, using `workflows/refactoring.md` and `agents/refactoring-orchestrator.md`.\n- resume: resume the paused WU only after the refactor-ticket is closed, superseded, or explicitly dispositioned by the active manager flavor with recorded evidence.\n- touched-file/component gate failures: this pause path does not alter touched-file/component ownership; current-WU `MEDIUM` or `HIGH` code-quality findings still revise, remediate, or decompose under the existing LOW-only rules.\n\n## Decision Recording\n\n<!-- INTENTIONAL: \"deferred\" here is a decision-recording state category, not an unwired workflow stub. -->\nIf a phase is skipped, narrowed, deferred, terminated for non-positive value, sent back to research on invalidated assumptions, or accepted with a named unverifiable residual risk that does not collapse the approved net-value case under the supported-surface termination rule:\n- record it in `${worktree_path}/DECISIONS.md` or an explicitly supplied project equivalent\n- record who made the decision\n- record why the change was accepted\n- record what risk is being accepted\n- record what evidence caused the termination or research re-entry\n\nFor Phase 6 firstness, do not create a new residual class. If a named test-verification risk remains unverified, record it in `risk/NN-test-residuals.md`. If only historical or process-provenance evidence is unverifiable and the approved net-value case still holds, record the decision only as `accepted with a named unverifiable residual risk` in `${worktree_path}/DECISIONS.md` or an explicitly supplied project equivalent.\n\nAccepted halt residuals and accepted `auditor_verdict_conflict_residual` entries follow this same Decision Recording rule when they do not collapse the approved net-value case.\n\nDecision Recording, generic residual recording, and Phase 7 / Phase 8 residual / value-zero review language do NOT authorize residual acceptance of Phase 4 code-quality, Phase 6 prototype-risk, or per-component code-quality `MEDIUM` or `HIGH` verdicts. Those gate verdicts revise, remediate, or decompose per `~/ai/conventions/code-quality.md` § `Disposition policy` and § `Oscillation signals WU-too-large`; they are never recorded as residuals. Generic residual recording remains valid for non-gate residual classes only (bounded test-verification residuals in `risk/NN-test-residuals.md`, process-provenance uncertainty per the Phase 6 firstness paragraph above, accepted halt residuals, accepted `auditor_verdict_conflict_residual` entries, and Phase 8 value-zero termination evidence).\n\nWithout that record, the phase was not skipped correctly.\n\n## Orchestrator\n\nThis pipeline is dispatched by the `implementation-pipeline-orchestrator` (`gpt-xhigh`) operator at `~/ai/agents/implementation-pipeline-orchestrator.md`. The orchestrator is the only delegated actor that walks a Work Unit through every phase, dispatches each leaf operator via the `agents` CLI, runs the three required process-tree audits, and enforces the violation-escalation policy autonomously (including Tier-1 main-branch rewinds when a violation is detected). Inlining the orchestrator role into the root conversation is itself a workflow violation because it removes the orchestration decisions from `agents trace --json` and prevents process-tree-auditor from auditing the workflow as a whole.\n\n## Adjacent References\n\n- `~/ai/agents/implementation-pipeline-orchestrator.md`\n- `~/ai/models/roles.md`\n- `~/ai/workflows/agents-cli.md`\n- `~/ai/conventions/worktree-isolation.md`\n- `~/ai/conventions/git.md`\n- `~/ai/agents/coderabbit-operator.md`\n- `~/ai/workflows/pr-review.md`\n- `~/ai/workflows/tiered-approval.md`\n- `~/ai/conventions/no-backwards-compatibility.md`\n- `~/ai/conventions/no-deferred-stubs.md`\n- `~/ai/conventions/gate-ownership.md`\n- `~/ai/conventions/audit-history.md`","lineStart":520,"lineEnd":652,"totalLines":652,"truncated":false}},"title":"../../../../ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md","time":{"start":1780750093117,"end":1780750093154}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e2676025ddb8b78016a24170d007081908401c0b0b7323ef3"}},"id":"prt_e9cfa0b2b001L3k7jZh0pVDxwN","sessionID":"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo","messageID":"msg_e9cf9dfd0001bvRJfAX4pcjTGk"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780750093168,"sessionID":"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_T2VYzWTHAcgRreCjhyf2gMHM","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs","offset":1,"limit":1000},"output":"<path>/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: use crate::generated::{\n2:     CONTRACT_VERSION, ErrorCategory, ErrorObject, ErrorResponseEnvelope, ProcessStatus,\n3: };\n4: use serde_json::Value;\n5: \n6: pub use crate::process::CapturedBytes;\n7: \n8: #[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]\n9: pub enum HostErrorKind {\n10:     SpawnFailed,\n11:     WaitFailed,\n12:     Timeout,\n13:     Cancelled,\n14:     UnknownSubcommand,\n15:     SchemaInvalidRequest,\n16:     SchemaInvalidResponse,\n17:     SchemaInvalidErrorResponse,\n18:     EmptyStdout,\n19:     InvalidUtf8,\n20:     InvalidJson,\n21:     NonObjectJson,\n22:     MultipleJsonObjects,\n23:     LeadingStdoutText,\n24:     TrailingNonWhitespace,\n25:     MismatchedContract,\n26:     MismatchedRequestId,\n27:     ProviderProcessNonzero,\n28:     ProviderProcessNonzeroWithSuccess,\n29:     ProviderClosedStdinEarly,\n30:     StdoutLimitExceeded,\n31:     MalformedLine,\n32:     UnknownEventKind,\n33:     SchemaInvalidEvent,\n34:     InvalidBase64,\n35:     DuplicateSeq,\n36:     SkippedSeq,\n37:     DecreasingSeq,\n38:     MissingFinalExit,\n39:     DuplicateExit,\n40:     EventAfterExit,\n41:     RuntimeDisabled,\n42:     MissingArtifact,\n43:     NotExecutable,\n44:     InvalidBinaryName,\n45:     UnsafeBinary,\n46:     Other(String),\n47: }\n48: \n49: impl HostErrorKind {\n50:     pub fn as_str(&self) -> &str {\n51:         match self {\n52:             Self::SpawnFailed => \"spawn_failed\",\n53:             Self::WaitFailed => \"wait_failed\",\n54:             Self::Timeo